# Emergency auto-release: pulses rATR with rACT held (rADR = direction); the
# firmware drives the fingers fully open or closed and ends force control.
# No latch: the gripper stays active and the next move_to works normally.
# After a fault the write only re-activates the gripper and the release is
# skipped (firmware >= v1.23) - call activate first, then emergency_release.

bool close_direction false   # false = release open, true = release close
---
bool success
string message
